    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d554">

                <pb facs="0776" n="766" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg766"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.893/12–1045</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State to President Truman
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-11">December 11,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There is attached the draft of a proposed letter to General Marshall for your
                        signature.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d554-f1"/> General Marshall, it is
                    understood, desires something in the form of a directive from you before his
                    departure and <pb facs="0777" n="767" xml:id="pg767"/> the attached letter has
                    been prepared in the Department of State with the thought of meeting General
                    Marshall’s desire.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> F. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d554-f1" n="34" xml:id="d554-f1-content">
                <p>For draft by Mr. Vincent revised by Mr. Byrnes on December 10, see <ref
                        target="#pg764">p. 764</ref>; for text signed December 15 by President
                    Truman, see <ref target="#pg770">p. 770</ref>. The enclosure was the revised
                    draft of Mr. Byrnes; this the President signed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
